# SPRINT: Product Import Pipeline — Implementation

**Goal:** Build simplest possible, robust pipeline for human-in-the-loop product scraping
**Duration:** 5-7 days
**Output:** Working CLI tool in `sang-logium-data/` workspace

---

## Pre-Flight Checklist

- [ ] Create `sang-logium-data/` folder adjacent to `sang-logium/`
- [ ] Initialize Node.js + TypeScript project
- [ ] Copy `catalogue-index.json` from main project
- [ ] Set up Sanity API credentials

---

## Phase 1: Foundation (Day 1)

### Setup Project Structure

```bash
cd c:\webdev
mkdir sang-logium-data
cd sang-logium-data
npm init -y
npm install typescript ts-node @types/node zod @sanity/client playwright dotenv
npx tsc --init
npx playwright install chromium
```

### Create Directory Structure

```
sang-logium-data/
├── plans/
├── scraped/
│   └── [plan-id]/
│       ├── batch-001.json
│       └── images/
├── validation/
├── uploads/
